<DocLayout
  title="Privacy Policy and Support · Home Stretch"
  description="Privacy Policy and support for Home Stretch: Moving Checklist on iPhone, iPad, and Android."
  eyebrow="Home Stretch"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  meta="Last updated: September 24, 2026"
  back={{ href: '/apps/home-stretch', label: 'Home Stretch' }}
>
  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Summary:</strong> Home Stretch does not collect, store, or transmit any personal data, on iPhone, iPad, or Android. Everything stays on your device.
  </div>

  <h2>Introduction</h2>
  <p>
    Home Stretch: Moving Checklist ("we", "our", or "the app") is a mobile app for iPhone, iPad, and Android,
    developed by Matt Donders. This Privacy Policy explains how the app handles your information on each platform.
  </p>

  <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
  <p><strong>None.</strong> Home Stretch does not collect any personal information. On every platform, the app:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Does not require an account or login</li>
    <li>Does not send your checklist anywhere</li>
    <li>Does not use analytics or tracking</li>
    <li>Does not display advertisements</li>
    <li>Does not access your contacts, location, camera, microphone, or any other device sensors</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Data Storage</h2>
  <p>
    Everything you create in the app (your move date, checklist progress, and your own tasks) is stored
    locally on your device: with Apple's SwiftData framework on iPhone and iPad, and in an on-device
    database on Android. This data is never sent to us or to any third party.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your device's own backup may include the app's data if you have it turned on: iCloud or computer
    backups on iPhone and iPad, and Android's backup to your Google account. Those backups are handled
    by Apple or Google, and we cannot access them.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you delete the app, its data is removed from your device.
  </p>

  <h2>In-App Purchases</h2>
  <p>
    Home Stretch offers a one-time in-app purchase to unlock the full checklist. On iPhone and iPad,
    payment is handled by Apple through the App Store. On Android, payment is handled by Google through
    Google Play. We do not collect, store, or have access to any payment information such as card
    numbers or billing details. The app only asks the store whether the purchase is active.
  </p>
  <p>
    For how your payment data is handled, see
    <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apple's Privacy Policy</a> or
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Home Stretch does not collect any data from anyone, including children. The app is safe for
    users of all ages.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
  <p>
    Home Stretch contains no third-party analytics, advertising, or tracking SDKs. The only outside
    service it talks to is the App Store or Google Play, to check your purchase.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be reflected on this
    page with an updated date.
  </p>

  <h2>Support and Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For help with Home Stretch or questions about this policy, email
    <a href="mailto:matt@mattdonders.com?subject=Home%20Stretch%20Support">matt@mattdonders.com</a>.
    Include your device, its iOS or Android version, and what happened. That is usually enough to work it out.
  </p>
  <h3>I bought the full checklist and it is not unlocked.</h3>
  <p>
    Open the app and tap <strong>Restore Purchases</strong>, signed in to the same Apple Account (iPhone and iPad)
    or Google Play account (Android) that made the purchase.
  </p>
  <h3>Refunds</h3>
  <p>
    Apple and Google handle purchases and refunds. For the App Store, go to
    <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>. For Google Play, see
    <a href="https://support.google.com/googleplay/answer/2479637">Google Play's refund page</a>.
  </p>
</DocLayout>
